        "date": "2026-11-21T01:21:17Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(motion): Bore gets a Helical strategy (one helix to the floor, then a floor circle)\n\nA Bore operation can now cut each hole with one continuous helix on the\nwall radius (the ring ladder's last ring) from the plunge height to the\nfloor, one flat floor circle, an optional spring pass, then a feed to the\ncentre and a retract. The pitch is the stepdown. There is no axial plunge.\n\nTwo refusals run before any move: a hole one helix cannot clear to the\ncentre (the message gives the core and the widest hole, twice the tool\ndiameter for a flat end mill), and a helix steeper than 15 deg (the\nmessage gives the pitch that fits). Detect holes skips and names the\nholes one helix cannot clear for a helical Bore.\n\nThe project file writes `helical` and `spring_pass` only when true, so a\nring ladder writes the same JSON and keeps its stamp. MCP lists the two\nfields. The Holes page gets a Strategy combo and a Spring pass check.\n\nFixes #2830\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
